BEGIN_HYPERDESC
<h1>Epsilon Eridani: the dust ring</h1>
A delta-glider 40 AU from Epsilon Eridani, a young K dwarf 10.5 light years
away, in the plane of the ring of dust that circles it at 69 AU (measured
by ALMA). The ring glows as a narrow band across the sky, several times
brighter than the Solar System's zodiacal light (Vulkan client). The gas
giant Epsilon Eridani b orbits at 3.5 AU.
END_HYPERDESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 61000.0
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship ERI-1
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET ERI-1
  MODE Extern
  POS 6.0 -160.0 -15
  TRACKMODE TargetRelative
  FOV 70.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_SHIPS
ERI-1:DeltaGlider
  STATUS Orbiting EpsilonEridani
  ELEMENTS 5.98e12 0.00000 74.8858 284.0717 0.0 0.0 61000.0
  AROT 0 0 0
  PRPLEVEL 0:1.000 1:1.000
END
END_SHIPS
